text:
The Source is an empty vessel,
Yet its potential can never be exhausted.
It is a bottomless abyss, the ancestor of all things.
It blunts the sharp iron blades;
It untangles the complex ciphers of the city;
It softens the glare of the blinding sun;
It settles the dust of the orange ridges.
It is completely hidden, yet it is always present.
I do not know whose child it is.
It existed before the first foundation was framed.

The universe is not sentimental;
It treats the empires and the empires' dust as the same shadow.
Sophia Rosetta Yolanda is not sentimental;
She treats the saint and the executioner with the same beauty.
The space between the sky and the ridge is like a bellows:
It is empty, yet it never collapses;
The more it moves, the more reality it breathes out.
Too many words lead only to exhaustion.
It is better to keep to the center of the Silence
